The TypeScript adaptation is the identity on frames: it has no writability
flag, so it forwards each validated input frame without a copy or allocation.
It refuses mode=random without an explicit seed (native draws one from
av_get_random_seed), numeric and expression mode values, the generic timeline
option enable, and runtime commands, and adds no FFmpeg runtime code.
The original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
